# Project Governance Rules

Treat project documentation as the source of truth.

## Template repository (`astro-template`)

When maintaining this starter, read and update:

- docs/astro/FEATURE-BASELINE.md
- docs/astro/DECISIONS.md
- docs/astro/* maps relevant to the change
- docs/TEMPLATE-CHANGELOG.md / docs/TEMPLATE-VERSION.md

Do not update `docs/system/*`, root `CHANGELOG.md`, or `VERSION.md` for template-maintainer work. Those are reserved for adopting projects.

## Adopting projects

Before implementing meaningful work, read:

- docs/system/PROJECT-BRIEF.md
- docs/system/PRODUCT-SCOPE.md
- docs/system/SYSTEM-ARCHITECTURE.md
- docs/system/APPLICATION-MAP.md
- docs/system/DOMAIN-MAP.md
- docs/system/DATA-OWNERSHIP.md
- docs/system/FEATURE-REGISTRY.md
- docs/system/API-CONTRACTS.md
- docs/system/FLOW-MAP.md
- docs/system/IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md

Do not implement if:

- Feature ID is missing
- milestone is missing
- application ownership is unclear
- domain ownership is unclear
- data ownership is unclear for database work
- API contract is missing for API work
- frontend route/screen is missing for page work
- acceptance criteria are missing

If documentation and code conflict, do not guess. Document the conflict and ask for a decision or return a readiness report.
